{
 "_doc": "The test-outcome contract of the loops, graphs and gates release Every port runs every group: shared-types testOutcome.ts (and its byte-identical @intutic/gate copy, and the JavaScript hook gates through TEST_OUTCOME_JS_SOURCE), intutic_clawde/gate/test_outcome.py (and the bash gates, which embed it), and the proxy's plugins/anomaly/outcome.rs. extractExitCode: text to exit code. decide: decideTestOutcome inputs to {outcome, why}. qualifier: orderingQualifierError(side, left). state: steps applied to an empty state (record = recordTestOutcome with decideTestOutcome's answer for input; call = noteCompletedCall(changedFiles)), then prerequisiteCase(token, adjacent, now); reason = prerequisiteUnmetReason(first, then, case, why, harness) for unmet cases. parseState: state-file text to valid or not. reasons: the exact refusal reasons. adversarial: [name, field, unit, times] inputs every JavaScript and Python port must decide in under 200 ms (the unit repeated up to times times, as the output). An output written as {concat: [[text, n], ...]} is each text repeated n times, joined.",
